WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.552
If the fitted line does not pass through every point, how does the algorithm decide which line is best?

00:00:06.552 --> 00:00:10.552
For each observation, the model makes a prediction.

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:16.057
The difference between the actual value and the predicted value is called a residual.

00:00:16.057 --> 00:00:23.112
If the actual value is ten and the prediction is nine point two, the residual is zero point eight.

00:00:23.572 --> 00:00:26.279
Run the code and inspect the residuals.

00:00:26.279 --> 00:00:33.169
The dashed vertical segments in the plot show the distance between each observed point and the fitted line.

00:00:33.169 --> 00:00:39.999
Machine learning algorithms often choose model parameters by minimizing some measure of overall error,

00:00:39.999 --> 00:00:45.339
called a loss function. You do not need to master optimization in this course.

00:00:45.339 --> 00:00:52.344
The important idea is that training means adjusting model parameters so predictions fit the training examples according

00:00:52.344 --> 00:00:54.115
to a defined objective.
